{
  "name": "stick-insect",
  "_about": "A stick-insect -- the Indian stick insect (Carausius morosus), 8.5 cm long: a twig; a long, thin, round body of segments with little knobs at the joints, no wings; a small head with short beaded antennae; the long thin forelegs stretched straight out ahead alongside the antennae, the four others thin and splayed; red at the base of the forelegs. Coats: brown, green. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
